Begin3
Title:          NTeX - A TeX distribution for Linux
Version:        1.2
Entered-date:   15-SEP-1994
Description:    NTeX is a TeX distribution containing TeX, MF, BibTeX etc. from
	        the web2c sources 6.1, xfig, MakeIndex, GLOTeX IDXTeX, xdvik,
                dvipsk, dviljk, texinfo, ... 
                Formats: plain TeX, extended plain TeX, AMSTeX, PicTeX,
                LaTeX2e (including AMSLaTeX, BABEL, SLITeX, ...), arabic,
                Devanagari, Greek, Hebrew, HieroTeX, Tamil, Turkish, Thai, ...
		Fonts: Sauter Computer Modern Fonts, DC (european fonts),
          	fc (african fonts), ...
Keywords:       ntex tex metafont latex amstex web2c typesetting
Author:         karl@cs.umb.edu (Karl Berry)
		phc@renoir.berkeley.edu (Pehong Chen)
		bvsmith@lbl.gov (Brian V. Smith)
		Donald Knuth
   		Leslie Lamport
   		Johannes Braams 
   		David Carlisle
   		Alan Jeffrey
   		Frank Mittelbach
   		Chris Rowley
		... 
		see the files AUTHORS, README and COPYING in the packages
 		for more
Maintained-by:  langbein@mathematik.uni-stuttgart.de (Frank Langbein)
Primary-site:   sunsite.unc.edu /pub/Linux/distributions/
		17 MB ntex/
Alternate-site: 
Original-site:  ftp.uni-stuttgart.de /tex-archive/
Platform:       xdvi needs ghostscript to display epsf files and postscript 
		fonts.
Copying-policy: Mainly GPL, for details refer to the notices in the single
		packages. Everything is freely distributable as long as the
  		notices are left intact and the contents of some files are
		not changed.
End

